WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.063
INFERIVA for commercial banks: an overview.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:09.397
Commercial banks run the whole financial crime function: onboarding, screening,

00:00:09.397 --> 00:00:14.526
monitoring, investigations and reporting. The pressure comes from two sides:

00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:19.991
alert volumes that outgrow the team, and correspondent banks asking for evidence,

00:00:19.991 --> 00:00:20.868
not policies.

00:00:21.867 --> 00:00:25.103
INFERIVA brings the function onto one customer record,

00:00:25.103 --> 00:00:27.021
so each step builds on the last,

00:00:27.021 --> 00:00:30.797
and the evidence is already joined up when someone asks for it.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.484
Monitoring rules cover large cash, cross-border transfers,

00:00:35.484 --> 00:00:39.994
politically exposed persons and structuring. Every change is versioned,

00:00:39.994 --> 00:00:42.789
so you can show what was running on any day.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.041
Alerts are prioritised in one queue, across customers, products and currencies.

00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:54.776
The analyst sees the customer's full activity, including cross-border wires,

00:00:54.776 --> 00:00:56.569
and who was on the other side.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:01.206
Fraud and money laundering are handled as one estate.

00:01:01.206 --> 00:01:05.878
A fraud alert shows the customer's money laundering risk and open cases,

00:01:05.878 --> 00:01:07.825
so nobody hears about it late.

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.716
Reports are drafted from the case, approved,

00:01:11.716 --> 00:01:14.764
and tracked until the regulator acknowledges them.

00:01:14.764 --> 00:01:18.666
The person who prepares a filing is not the person who sends it.

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:22.156
Every action is in the audit trail.

00:01:22.156 --> 00:01:27.324
When a correspondent or an examiner asks what happened, the answer is a record,

00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:28.697
not a reconstruction.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:34.809
Onboarding, monitoring, fraud, cases and filing, on one customer record.

00:01:34.809 --> 00:01:40.195
So when a correspondent or an examiner asks, the evidence is already joined up.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.071
To see it for your institution, talk to INFERIVA.
